        "original_id": "14220ef1-1d88-5a9a-bd40-1f9dd437cea5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alexander Hall, Jon Amiel, Ida Lupino, Henry Roquemore\n- Works: Yours for the Asking, Meet John Doe, The Little Foxes, The Magnificent Ambersons\n- Roles: film director, theatre actor\n- Topics: film and television, Western movies\n\nFacts:\n- Alexander Hall was born on January 11, 1894, in Boston, Massachusetts, and he died on July 30, 1968, in San Francisco, California.\n- Alexander Hall was an American film director and theatre actor.\n- Jon Amiel was born on 20 May 1948.\n- Jon Amiel is an English film director who has worked in film and television in both the UK and the US since the early 1980s.\n- Yours for the Asking was directed by Alexander Hall and also featured Ida Lupino.\n- Henry Roquemore played many uncredited roles in Western movies.\n- Henry Roquemore appeared in the major films Meet John Doe, The Little Foxes, The Magnificent Ambersons, and the Marx Brothers film Yours for the Asking.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
