        "text": "Page: Alexander Hall. Sentence: Alexander Hall (January 11, 1894, Boston, Massachusetts – July 30, 1968, San Francisco, California) was an American film director and theatre actor.\nPage: Jon Amiel. Sentence: Jon Amiel (born 20 May 1948) is an English film director who has since the early 1980s worked in film and television in both the UK and the US.\nPage: Yours for the Asking. Sentence: The movie also features Ida Lupino and was directed by Alexander Hall.\nPage: Henry Roquemore. Sentence: Many of his roles were uncredited parts in Western movies, but he also appeared in major films including \"Meet John Doe\", \"The Little Foxes\", \"The Magnificent Ambersons\", and the Marx Brothers film \"Yours for the Asking\".",
